/* FluffOS PORT NOTE: this driver build's compiled binary does not expose
 * query_ed_mode() as an efun even though it's declared in the FluffOS
 * source tree (packages/core/core.spec, gated behind F_QUERY_ED_MODE) --
 * "Undefined function query_ed_mode" at compile time. This is critical:
 * global/prompt.lpc's write_prompt() and global/process_input.lpc's
 * process_input() both call it on every single line a connected player
 * sends, to decide whether raw input should be routed to the line editor
 * (ed_start()/ed_cmd(), which ARE present in this driver build) instead
 * of normal command processing -- without some definition here, those
 * two core files fail to compile at all, breaking every player's prompt/
 * input handling, not just the editor.
 *
 * in_edit(object), which IS available in this driver build, reports
 * whether an object is currently in an ed session (returns the filename
 * being edited, or 0). That's enough to preserve the actually-critical
 * behavior (this != -1 gate that routes input to ed_cmd() while editing)
 * even though the driver's real query_ed_mode() also distinguishes finer
 * sub-states (0 = normal ed prompt, -2 = "more" pagination prompt, N =
 * prompting to insert at line N) that aren't recoverable from in_edit()
 * alone -- callers here always see 0 (normal) while editing, so the
 * editor works correctly, but the "more:" pagination prompt text
 * (prompt.lpc's case -2) never shows during simple output paging inside
 * ed; a cosmetic loss, not a functional one.
 */
int query_ed_mode() {
  if (in_edit(previous_object()))
    return 0;
  return -1;
} /* query_ed_mode() */
